## The Landing

::bg{location="skerry_landing" time="morning"}
::music{action="start" mood="tense" volume="down"}
@narrator: The boat noses against the iron steps of Skerry Rock. Spray comes over the gunwale in sheets.
::auto{character="hollis" anchor="left" action="fadeInUp"}
@hollis: This is as close as I go, Inspector. The Board pays me to ferry, not to drown.
@hollis{when="has(prev.run.verdictFate) && prev.run.verdictFate != 'fell'"}: They sent you back, then. The last report satisfied nobody.
@inspector: When did anyone last see the light burning?
@hollis{emotion="sad"}: Burned at dusk on the fourteenth, like always. By two bells it was dark. By morning it was lit again, and Elias Voss was gone.
@inspector{mono}: Dark, then lit again. A lamp does not relight itself.
<branch id="firstQuestion" prompt="Hollis is already casting off.">
  <choice id="askBoat" label="Ask about the wrecked boat">
    @hollis: The Guillemot. Tobias Crane's. Came ashore in pieces on the north side. Folk are saying things about Tobias.
    ::assert{implicates(guillemot, tobias)}
  </choice>
  <choice id="askAda" label="Ask about the assistant keeper">
    @hollis: Ada Pell. Ashore sick that week, at her aunt's. Lucky girl, some say.
  </choice>
</branch>
::clear
@narrator: The boat pulls away. You are alone on the rock with a dark lantern and a logbook nobody has opened.
